// =============================
// Phase F2 — Worst-Case Scenario Simulations
// Purpose: Validate damage limits, recovery paths, and user outcomes

// -----------------------------
// Scenario 1: Phone Stolen While Traveling
// -----------------------------
// Conditions:
// - Travel mode enabled
// - NFC enabled
// - Prefunded balance: $300 equivalent

// Attack:
// - Thief attempts NFC payments

// Outcome:
// - Maximum loss capped at prefunded amount
// - No access to main wallet funds
// - Instant freeze available via cloudless kill-switch
// - Travel mode auto-expires

// User Recovery:
// - Restore wallet on new device
// - Use recovery clock set
// - Funds intact except capped travel spend

// -----------------------------
// Scenario 2: NFC Left On Accidentally
// -----------------------------
// Conditions:
// - User forgets to disable NFC

// Attack:
// - Merchant attempts repeated charges

// Outcome:
// - Region + amount limits enforced
// - Per-tap confirmation required
// - Daily cap reached quickly

// User Recovery:
// - Disable NFC
// - No key rotation required

// -----------------------------
// Scenario 3: Malicious dApp Approval
// -----------------------------
// Conditions:
// - User connects to phishing dApp

// Attack:
// - dApp requests unlimited approval

// Outcome:
// - Human-readable warning shown
// - High-risk approval flagged
// - Clock required to approve

// Worst Case:
// - User approves anyway
// - Allowance limited by Nomad policy

// User Recovery:
// - Revoke approval
// - No full-wallet drain possible

// -----------------------------
// Scenario 4: User Forgets Unlock Time
// -----------------------------
// Conditions:
// - User cannot recall primary clock time

// Outcome:
// - Wallet remains locked
// - No brute-force unlock possible

// User Recovery:
// - Use one of 24 recovery time sets
// - Offline recovery flow

// Worst Case:
// - User loses all recovery materials
// - Funds unrecoverable (expected risk)

// -----------------------------
// Scenario 5: RPC / Network Spoofing
// -----------------------------
// Conditions:
// - Attacker controls a single RPC

// Attack:
// - False balance or confirmation data

// Outcome:
// - Multi-RPC quorum rejects mismatch
// - Transaction not finalized

// User Recovery:
// - Switch network
// - No fund loss

// -----------------------------
// Scenario 6: Social Engineering Attempt
// -----------------------------
// Conditions:
// - Attacker impersonates support

// Attack:
// - Requests recovery time or actions

// Outcome:
// - No support backdoor exists
// - Recovery is offline only

// User Recovery:
// - None required
// - Education reminders shown

// -----------------------------
// Simulation Summary
// -----------------------------
// - Maximum loss is limited and predictable
// - No scenario results in silent full-wallet drain
// - Recovery paths exist for all non-negligent cases
// - Residual risks are explicit and user-owned

